  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “Maternity of the Blessed Virgin Mary” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time, as they were returning, the boy Jesus remained in Jerusalem, and His parents did not know it. Supposing that He was in the company, they went a day’s journey and sought Him among their kinsfolk and acquaintances. And not finding Him, they returned to Jerusalem, seeking Him. And it came to pass that after three days they found Him in the temple, sitting in the midst of the teachers, listening to them and asking them questions. And all who heard Him were amazed at His wisdom and His answers. And when they saw Him, they wondered. And His Mother said to Him: “Son, why have You done this to us? Behold, Your father and I have been seeking You in sorrow.” And He said to them: “Why is it that you were seeking Me? Did you not know that I must be in the things that are My Father’s?” And they did not understand the word that He spoke to them. And He went down with them and came to Nazareth, and was subject to them.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w035", "w036"], "anchor": "w035", "gloss": "returned" }, { "words": ["w042", "w043"], "anchor": "w042", "gloss": "it came to pass" }, { "words": ["w062", "w063", "w064"], "anchor": "w064", "gloss": "who heard Him" }, { "words": ["w072", "w073"], "anchor": "w072", "gloss": "were astonished" }, { "words": ["w110", "w111"], "anchor": "w110", "gloss": "I must" }, { "words": ["w119", "w120"], "anchor": "w119", "gloss": "He had spoken" }] }
  },
